			],
			"Message": "style(Output): Normalize shell script indentation and case formatting\n\nAdjust indentation in Source/Run.sh and Source/prepublishOnly.sh to use consistent spacing in case statements and branch bodies. The logic and behavior remain unchanged — only whitespace and formatting are modified.\n\nThis improves readability and consistency across the Output component's build scripts.",
			"SHA": "3114a2923ddf9279fcb94033a406756bb39053bd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T20:20:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠀⠀⠀",
				769,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Restructure ESBuild configuration and plugin system to flat layout\n\nThe nested `Configuration/Element/Output/Source/` directory was the authoritative source for the Output component's ESBuild build pipeline, but the compiled `.js`/`.js.map` artifacts lived in `Configuration/` alongside them. This created a split-source problem where generated outputs and hand-authored sources were interleaved, making reproducible builds and source-level debugging difficult.\n\nThis commit flattens the structure:\n- Delete the entire `Configuration/Element/Output/Source/` tree (ESBuild configs, 50+ transform plugins, polyfills, CEL services, TypeScript configs)\n- Promote all source modules to `Configuration/` root with `.js`/`.js.map` pairs for direct consumption\n- Move `Source/ESBuild/Microsoft/VSCode.ts` to `Configuration/ESBuild/Microsoft/VSCode.js` (compiled output)\n- Add `Source/prepublishOnly.sh` for npm packaging\n- Add `outbase` to VSCode ESBuild config so `vs/base/common/uri.js` lands at `Target/Microsoft/VSCode/vs/base/common/uri.js` instead of the full Dependency path\n\nThe ESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via `Compiler=Rest`), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via `Clean=true`, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS Code's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility. Cocoon continues to consume fresh builds from `Configuration/` at runtime via the existing pipeline.\n\nThis ensures the repository tracks only source-of-truth configuration while enabling reproducible builds, source-level debugging of the build pipeline, and version-controlled evolution of the Output component's bundling logic.",
			"SHA": "1ad957d3d880fdab47dbad105b1cc901f16901d0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T15:21:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				963,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Update bundled artifacts and source modules\n\n- Minify Shared/Process/Proxy.js IIFE parameter names (no logic changes)\n- Add property access brackets in Identity.ts product replacement definitions\n- Add type annotations to Tauri main process service for VSCode event types\n\nNo functional or behavioral changes. Improves compression minification and type safety.",
			"SHA": "9e323902d9d5c937517060c07f1064ed2ac622ad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T15:14:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				963,
				137
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): implement complete ESBuild configuration and plugin system\n\nAdd the complete set of ESBuild configuration modules and plugin pipeline source files to Configuration/.\n\nThis includes:\n- ESBuild entry configurations (CodeEditorLand/Editor, CodeEditorLand/Editor, Microsoft/VSCode variants)\n- Plugin pipeline modules (Apply, Copy, Polyfill, Transform namespaces with 50+ transforms)\n- Runtime polyfills (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPC/Renderer, SharedProcess, Process, Telemetry)\n- CEL services (ExposeAccessor, TauriMainProcess with MistWebSocketTransport)\n\nAlso add TypeScript composite project configs and polyfill modules.\n\nThe ESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via Compiler=Rest), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via Clean=true, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS Code's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility.",
			"SHA": "7604d0318d8f169635792e2a50980d77f0f64453"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T15:03:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				656,
				126
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): implement Output component ESBuild configuration and pipeline\n\nAdd the complete ESBuild build system source to Configuration/ including: ESBuild entry configurations (Editor, VSCode, Bundle variants), exclusion rule modules (Bootstrap, Electron, Node, Network, Telemetry, Test, Types, WebWorker, Workbench, and Chromium IPC), plugin pipeline (Apply, Copy, Polyfill, Transform namespaces with 50+ transforms), runtime polyfills (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPC/Renderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcessProxy, Telemetry), and CEL services (ExposeAccessor, ExtensionsScanner, NullExtensionGallery, NullTelemetry, NullUpdate, Search, SharedProcess, DevLog, TauriMainProcess with MistWebSocketTransport, Trace). Also add TypeScript composite project configs for CodeEditorLand/Editor and Microsoft/VSCode targets.\n\nThese modules were previously only present as compiled .js/.js.map outputs in Configuration/ - the authoritative source now lives in the repository enabling reproducible builds, source-level debugging of the build pipeline, and version-controlled evolution of the Output component's bundling logic. The ESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via Compiler=Rest), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via Clean=true, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS Code's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility.",
			"SHA": "d2876e62d1224ae346a27e4d080c5b2f9f0c053f"
		}
	],
